; The trolls talk about cooking the player
;
; Script handler (op 3, in the script #R$CA3B of both trolls). When the player
; is at the trolls clearing (LOC_TROLLS_CLEARING) the speaking troll says
; "Blimey, look at this!! Can yer cook'em?" (the hideous troll) or "Yer can try,
; but he wouldn't make above a mouthfull" (the vicious troll). Elsewhere it
; returns before the test pass accepts, and the script repeats.
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
@label=TrollsTalk
c$A9BD LD A,($B6F5)  ; player's location
@isub=CP LOC_TROLLS_CLEARING
 $A9C0 CP $05
 $A9C2 RET NZ        ; not at the clearing: refuse
 $A9C3 CALL $9D44
 $A9C6 LD A,($B6EA)  ; the troll speaking
 $A9C9 LD HL,$B238   ; "Blimey, look at this!! Can yer cook'em?"
@isub=CP CHR_HIDEOUS_TROLL
 $A9CC CP $47
 $A9CE JR Z,$A9D3
 $A9D0 LD HL,$B24C   ; "Yer can try, but he wouldn't make above a mouthfull"
*$A9D3 JP $A1E3
